In <1993Oct14.092945.27663@beaver.cs.washington.edu> peg@cs.washington.edu writes:

> In general, I like the new feature that allows monsters to use their
> treasure (scrolls, potions, and wands). However, some of the wands are
> just too powerful. I have lost some very good characters to monsters
> that had wands of sleep, fire, and death. Just a moment ago, my 13th
> level Valkyrie, with an AC of -9, +4 longsword, and gauntlets of power
> got zapped by an elf of some sort with a wand of death! I've also lost
> a barbarian on the quest, because some ogre had a wand of sleep. He
> put me to sleep, and a horde of ogres gathered around and gradually
> beat me to a pulp (*very* gradually -- if I remember right, I had 100+
> hit points, and an AC below -10).
> 
> There doesn't seem to be any way of beating this -- If it has the
> wand, you're going to die, unless you are somehow able to outrun the
> monster and get off the level. In order to fight, you have to get in
> its line of sight. Sometimes you can't run away without getting in its
> line of sight.
> 
> The only thing that can save you in this situation is the amulet of
> reflection, and those don't come along very often.
> 
> It just seems like monsters should not have the "certain death" items
> like this.

Moats are certain death too, but there is a chance that you can teleport
out of them (if you have a teleport spell, and don't have an amulet of
breathing or levitation of some sort).  Perhaps there should be the same
sort of chance to teleport out of the path of a magical effect, with
some slight effect (ie if you teleport from a sleep ray, you sleep for 2-6
turns instead of a hundred or whatever).

